    [3:5-4:22] if (cmp (call crop) == None)
      [4:9-4:22] (expr (call plant RADISH))
  [5:1-5:11] (= x (// 10 2))
  [8:1-8:9] (return x)
  [9:1-9:6] (break)
  [10:1-12:13] def outer()
    [11:5-12:13] def inner()
      [12:9-12:13] (pass)
  [16:1-17:14] while True
    [17:5-17:14] (= stray 1)
  [18:1-18:7] (= ok 1)
--- diagnostics ---
E-MISSING-COLON 2:10-2:11 This \`def\` line needs a \`:\` at the end.
E-ASSIGN-IN-IF 3:15-3:16 Use \`==\` to compare. A single \`=\` stores a value.
E-SLASH-DIVISION 5:8-5:9 Sprout uses whole numbers. Use \`//\` for division.
E-NO-POWER 6:7-6:9 Sprout has no \`**\`. Multiply the number by itself instead.
E-NO-FLOAT 7:5-7:8 Sprout uses whole numbers, so \`1.5\` can't be used.
E-RETURN-OUTSIDE 8:1-8:7 \`return\` only works inside a function made with \`def\`.
E-BREAK-OUTSIDE 9:1-9:6 \`break\` only works inside a loop.
E-NESTED-DEF 11:5-11:8 Define functions at the top level, not inside other functions or blocks.
E-BAD-TARGET 13:1-13:4 You can only store a value in a name or a list/dict slot.
E-UNEXPECTED-TOKEN 14:1-14:6 I didn't expect \`12abc\` here.
E-UNEXPECTED-TOKEN 15:15-15:16 I didn't expect \`]\` here.
E-BAD-INDENT 16:13-16:17 The lines inside this \`while\` should be indented one step further."
`;

